const e={"seo.purpose":"Who the red-envelope notes are for","seo.purpose.p1":"People deciding what to give at a wedding, a baby’s first month, or Lunar New Year who want one cited figure, without treating one article as a rule.","seo.purpose.p2":"Also for separating a company year-end party from a gift you bring yourself.","seo.why":"Why these notes","seo.why.p1":"Every figure points back to a dated Taiwan article, with the link on the page.","seo.why.li1":"Gifts you give and packets a company hands out are separate. The party is not compared with a wedding rate.","seo.why.li2":"Pick the occasion and who it is for, and the reference amount appears. Nothing to type. Weddings also offer a gift-only, not-attending option.","seo.why.li3":"None of the listed amounts contains a 4. An odd ending is only noted as something some people notice, not as a ban.","seo.why.p2":"Everything is shown in the browser. Nothing is sent anywhere.","seo.faq":"Red envelope questions","seo.faq.q1":"Are these amounts required?","seo.faq.q1a":"No. The source articles say relationships, regions, and budgets differ.","seo.faq.q2":"Why do newborn figures disagree?","seo.faq.q2a":"The Parenting.com.tw article’s table and its prose are not identical. This page uses the table’s span as the reference and says so.","seo.faq.q3":"How much should a company give at the year-end party?","seo.faq.q3a":"There is no published standard amount. The labor ministry has described those gifts as benefits, not wages.","seo.faq.q4":"Do I have to follow the lucky-number notes?","seo.faq.q4a":"No. Two cited articles retell a custom of avoiding 4. That note does not change the amounts in their tables, and this page does not tell you to switch to another amount.","seo.faq.q5":"How much for a gift when you are not attending?","seo.faq.q5a":"The nationwide 104 table has no gift-only row. The starting amounts here come from Roo.Cash (2026-03-17): NT$1,200 and up for restaurants and banquet halls, NT$1,600 and up for five-star hotels. That source does not split by relationship."};export{e as default};
